{
  "browser_run": "not performed by this record; G0 asks for a Copernicus COG read from a browser origin with the CORS result recorded (PRD 9), which this header evidence implies but does not replace",
  "cop30_mode_note": "cop30_mode (direct or proxy) is chosen by the team at G0 (PRD 9, PRD 15 architecture review); this record is evidence for that choice and does not set it, and T1-07 writes it nowhere, config/run.yaml included",
  "cors_evidence_reasons": [
    "https://example.org: the preflight answered HTTP 403, not 2xx",
    "https://example.org: the preflight response has no Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or *",
    "https://example.org: the preflight response has no Access-Control-Allow-Methods listing GET or *",
    "https://example.org: the preflight response has no Access-Control-Allow-Headers listing range or *",
    "https://example.org: the Range GET response has no Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or *, so a browser's CORS check would fail",
    "https://example.org: Access-Control-Expose-Headers on the Range GET does not list Content-Range and is not *",
    "https://example.org: Access-Control-Expose-Headers on the Range GET does not list Accept-Ranges and is not *",
    "http://localhost:3000: the preflight answered HTTP 403, not 2xx",
    "http://localhost:3000: the preflight response has no Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or *",
    "http://localhost:3000: the preflight response has no Access-Control-Allow-Methods listing GET or *",
    "http://localhost:3000: the preflight response has no Access-Control-Allow-Headers listing range or *",
    "http://localhost:3000: the Range GET response has no Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or *, so a browser's CORS check would fail",
    "http://localhost:3000: Access-Control-Expose-Headers on the Range GET does not list Content-Range and is not *",
    "http://localhost:3000: Access-Control-Expose-Headers on the Range GET does not list Accept-Ranges and is not *"
  ],
  "cors_evidence_scope": "the GLO-30 tile URL, which bears on cop30_mode; each URL's own value is under urls[].cors_evidence_supports",
  "cors_evidence_supports": "proxy_needed",
  "derivation_rule": "Per URL, over every origin tested. direct_read: the preflight answers 2xx with Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or *, Access-Control-Allow-Methods listing GET or *, and Access-Control-Allow-Headers listing range or *; and the Range GET answers 206 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or * and Access-Control-Expose-Headers listing Content-Range and Accept-Ranges or being *. proxy_needed: for every origin the Range GET's response has no single Access-Control-Allow-Origin equal to the origin or *, so a browser's CORS check fails and script cannot read the response (Fetch standard, CORS check). inconclusive: anything else. A missing header counts as absent, never as allowing. The top-level value is the GLO-30 URL's, which bears on cop30_mode; the WorldCover URL's value bears on the live WorldCover check (PRD 8.7 step 4).",
  "description": "Origin-header requests to one Copernicus GLO-30 tile and one ESA WorldCover map (the tiles the T1-06 and wc records read), with the response headers that decide whether a browser may read them cross-origin (PRD 8.7 step 2 and 4; 9 G0; 15 architecture review). Raw observations and a derived evidence value only: the G0 status and cop30_mode are human decisions (PRD 23.6).",
  "method": {
    "absent_header": "a header the response does not carry is recorded with state absent and no values, and never counts as allowing",
    "client": "io.send_http_exchange: Host, Accept-Encoding: identity and the request headers listed per request; no User-Agent, cookie, credential or project identifier; redirects are not followed",
    "error_message": "body.error_message quotes the <Message> of an XML <Error> body as the server sent it, else null; the body itself is at body.local_path",
    "headers_that_matter": [
      "access-control-allow-origin",
      "access-control-allow-methods",
      "access-control-allow-headers",
      "access-control-expose-headers",
      "access-control-max-age",
      "vary",
      "content-range",
      "accept-ranges",
      "content-length"
    ],
    "origins": [
      {
        "key": "neutral",
        "origin": "https://example.org",
        "why": "a neutral HTTPS origin reserved for documentation (example.org), so no project or personal name is sent"
      },
      {
        "key": "localhost",
        "origin": "http://localhost:3000",
        "why": "a local development origin, as a browser on a developer's machine would send it"
      }
    ],
    "requests": {
      "preflight": "OPTIONS with Origin, Access-Control-Request-Method: GET and Access-Control-Request-Headers: range",
      "range_get": "GET with Origin and Range: bytes=0-1023"
    },
    "statement": "This is a server-side request that sends an Origin header (Python http.client through io.send_http_exchange), not a real browser fetch. The header evidence implies but does not replace a browser run: a browser applies its own CORS checks, caching and preflight rules, which this record does not observe."
  },
